{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["And because he said <b>permanent redemption</b>, he said <b>and that which shall be redeemed</b>. The meaning is like <b>he shall acquire</b>. Some say: even if the redeemer were a Levite. The vav of <b>veyatza</b> [ותצא] is like a weak fa in the language of Ishmael. <b>House</b> or <b>city</b> — the legal ruling is one. [n: The Hebrew reads ויצא in the lemma but the verse form is ותצא (feminine); Ibn Ezra addresses the vav where the standard form has none. 'Weak fa' refers to Arabic dialectal pronunciation of qamatz/qamatz-like vowels.]"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:27.810183146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}